 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "And May is all sweet the flower\nThat makes the dawn so tender.\nGod, for whose heart from dower and fire\nIn these long years hath neither,\nNought as the glad lark's nigh voice sings aloud\nFrom the loud bells of heaven to our\nSprung white hands in love as one's own fire\nSinging them anew as now or higher.\nXXIII. In vernal days of summer\nI heard a bird cry above,\nEchoing out like death upon our\nFar-troped home; then afar",
